# SDL2

It lives here rather than under libraries/ because
docs/modules-libraries.mdy says so: "A library that implements one platform
lives with that platform rather than here." Pico SDK is the other instance.
platforms/linux/mm.mdy carries the option: core no and read-only: core that a
library branch needs, which is the condition that rule attaches.

An installed system package rather than a vendored tree. source names a
directory that records what was observed rather than a copy of SDL's source,
because SDL2 here comes from the distribution and copying it would be a
pretence. The checkout rules still apply to that directory, so an absent record
is reported the way any absent checkout is.

Its whole declared interface is one link input. No include-directory is needed:
SDL2's headers sit at their package-qualified path under a default search
directory, so a wrapper including <SDL2/SDL.h> compiles with no -I, which was
measured rather than assumed.

The licence is the distribution's copyright file for the package this names.
SDL2 is zlib-licensed.
